<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher mark: the shield with a keyhole, drawn at launcher scale rather than borrowed from it.

  This used to be LkIcons.Shield's 24×24 path under a `scaleX/Y="2.6"` group. That kept the two marks
  provably identical, which was the right instinct and the wrong execution: a glyph authored for 24dp
  has a 24dp detail budget, and blowing it up 2.6× spends none of the room a 108dp canvas offers. The
  silhouette here is the same shield to within a rounding — same shoulder angle, same 0.86 width-to-
  height, same keyhole proportions — so it still reads as one mark, but it is authored in the 108 grid
  so the surface can carry a bevel, a light, and a punched hole.

  Four things the scaled version could not have:

   1. *An edge.* A lit rim along the silhouette, brightest at the apex and gone by the waist. This is
      what stops the mark reading as a flat sticker on a flat ground.
   2. *A surface.* A light over the top-left facet and a shade over the bottom, both clipped to the
      shield, on the same light source as the background and as LkScreen's aura.
   3. *A hole that is a hole.* The keyhole is knocked out three times: a dark offset up-left, a lit
      jade offset down-right, then the true opening on top. What survives is a shadow crescent on the
      near wall and a lit crescent on the far one — the read of something cut *through* a plate.
   4. *No seam.* The old keyhole was a circle subpath plus a stem subpath that overlapped, under
      `evenOdd` — so the lens where they crossed cancelled to zero and filled with shield colour, a
      jade wedge sitting in the middle of the opening. Invisible at 24dp, not at 108. It is now a
      single continuous outline: down the stem, round its foot, back up, then the long way over the
      circle. One subpath cannot cancel against itself.

  Geometry: centred on (54, 54), spanning x 27.9–80.1 and y 23.6–84.4. Furthest point from centre is
  the top-right shoulder at 32.46, inside the adaptive icon's 33 safe radius with room for the mask.

  === v2, 2026-07-31 ===============================================================================
  Two changes, both checked against the adaptive mask; the technique above is untouched.

   1. Scaled +7% about (54,54). The silhouette's furthest point moves from 30.3 to 32.46 of the 33
      safe radius, so the mark fills the tile instead of floating in it. Same shoulders, same 0.86
      width-to-height — it is the same shield.
   2. Keyhole enlarged past the uniform scale: radius 6.1 to 7.0, stem half-width 2.3 to 2.6, foot
      dropped to y63. The punch now reads on the 48dp launcher grid and at 19dp in the drawer.
      Still one continuous single-subpath outline, so point 4 above still holds.

  This drawing is also what the app renders in-app: LkLogo's LkMark is this silhouette and keyhole
  flattened onto the 24 grid.

  === 1a "Slim & sharp", 2026-09-07 ===============================================================
  The lighting is now `site/Vault App Landing Design/assets/icon-slim.svg`, the option picked out of
  the Icon Lab: harder light, brighter rim, crisper keyhole. **No geometry moved.** The silhouette,
  the keyhole and their proportions are byte-for-byte what v2 left, because 1a changed nothing about
  them either — diffed against `assets/logo-compact.svg`, the mark 1a was offered as a refinement of,
  the shield path and the keyhole path are character-identical in both. Only the surface changed, so
  ic_launcher_monochrome.xml and LkMark — which carry the silhouette with no surface at all — need no
  edit to stay the same mark.

  Five surface changes, each traceable to a line of the SVG:

   1. *Plate.* #78F5D3/#39D4AA/#159576 -> #83F8D6/#31D0A5/#0E8A6B: brighter at the apex, deeper at
      the foot, so the plate itself carries more of the modelling.
   2. *Light.* The soft radial haze is gone. 1a lights the shield with an angular facet — a triangle
      from the apex down the left shoulder, under its own white .22 -> 0 gradient — which is what
      gives the mark a hard edge of light instead of a bloom. This is the single biggest change.
   3. *Crown.* A new white .4 stroke tracing the shield's top two edges, inside the clip. v2 had no
      such line; it is what makes the top read as a chamfer rather than a fold.
   4. *Rim.* The evenOdd band (silhouette minus a 0.9 inset) is replaced by 1a's actual construction,
      a stroke on the silhouette itself, and made much brighter: #F2FFFB at .9 where the band peaked
      at .46, fading through #AEFFE9 .2 and reaching zero at y63 rather than y54.
   5. *Keyhole.* Shadow and lit offsets both pulled in — (-5,-7)/(6,8) -> (-3,-4)/(4,5) in SVG units
      — so the crescents are tighter and the punch reads as thinner stock; and a specular arc is
      added inside the opening's upper-left, the highlight of light caught on the far wall.

  Mapping, since the two canvases are not a simple divide. The SVG shield spans x 92–420, y 84–462
  inside a 512 box; this one spans x 27.9–80.1, y 23.6–84.4 inside 108 — a *relatively larger* mark,
  which is what v2's +7% bought and is not given back here. So every feature that lives on the shield
  is mapped through the shield's own bounding box rather than through the canvas:

      x' = 54 + (x - 256) * 0.15915        y' = 23.6 + (y - 84) * 0.16085

  Stroke widths take the same factor (7 -> 1.11), except inside the keyhole group, where the SVG's
  own scale(0.786) applies first (7 -> 0.88). The keyhole offsets are scaled by 0.786 for the same
  reason before being mapped.

  One deliberate deviation: 1a's rim stroke is 7 units, which maps to 1.11, and a centred stroke puts
  half of that outside the silhouette — 32.46 + 0.555 = 33.02, a hair past the 33 safe radius the
  comment above claims. It is set to 1.0 instead, which lands at 32.96 and keeps that claim true. The
  0.11 difference is under a tenth of a dp at launcher size and invisible; a false safe-radius claim
  would not be.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:aapt="http://schemas.android.com/aapt"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!--
      === Proportion, corrected 2026-09-07 =========================================================
      The background maps 1a into the 108 grid at 36/247 = 0.14575. The mapping above uses 0.15915,
      the 9.2% enlargement inherited from v2 and knowingly kept. On an actual launcher the two
      factors do not read as one drawing: the shield took 72.5% of the visible 72dp tile where 1a
      takes 66.4% of its own, and since the mark is centred here but seated low there, nearly all of
      the difference came off the top — 7.8% margin against 15.2%. Under a circle mask the shoulder
      ran to 90% of the mask radius and the lit ground vanished behind the shield, which is the one
      thing the plate-on-a-lit-ground reading depends on.

      Rather than re-derive every coordinate at 0.14575, the drawing is scaled whole. 0.916 is
      0.664/0.725, the exact width 1a has; translateY 2.45 restores its seating, since 1a's shield
      centre sits at 53.4% of the tile from the top rather than 50%. A group transform carries the
      stroke widths with it, which is what the mapping note above wants in any case.

      Measured after, against the visible 18..90 tile, with 1a's own figures beside them:
          left/right margin  16.8%   (1a: 16.8%)
          top margin         14.7%   (1a: 15.2%)
          bottom margin       7.9%   (1a:  8.3%)
      The furthest point is now the bottom tip at 30.3 from centre, 30.8 with half the rim stroke —
      so the 33 safe radius the note above is careful about gets more headroom, not less, and the
      shoulder that used to define the extreme drops from 32.96 to 28.4.
    -->
    <group
        android:pivotX="54"
        android:pivotY="54"
        android:scaleX="0.916"
        android:scaleY="0.916"
        android:translateY="2.45">

    <!-- The plate. -->
    <path android:pathData="M54 23.6 L80.1 34.7 V54.3 c0 16.14 -11.17 27 -26.1 30.1 c-14.94 -3.1 -26.1 -13.96 -26.1 -30.1 V34.7 Z">
        <aapt:attr name="android:fillColor">
            <gradient
                android:startX="33.95"
                android:startY="26.82"
                android:endX="73.73"
                android:endY="83.11"
                android:type="linear">
                <item android:offset="0" android:color="#FF83F8D6" />
                <item android:offset="0.46" android:color="#FF31D0A5" />
                <item android:offset="1" android:color="#FF0E8A6B" />
            </gradient>
        </aapt:attr>
    </path>

    <!-- Surface modelling, clipped to the plate. -->
    <group>
        <clip-path android:pathData="M54 23.6 L80.1 34.7 V54.3 c0 16.14 -11.17 27 -26.1 30.1 c-14.94 -3.1 -26.1 -13.96 -26.1 -30.1 V34.7 Z" />

        <!-- The lit facet: apex, left shoulder, and down the left flank. -->
        <path android:pathData="M54 23.6 L30.13 34.22 L34.9 67.99 Z">
            <aapt:attr name="android:fillColor">
                <gradient
                    android:startX="37.13"
                    android:startY="24.57"
                    android:endX="65.78"
                    android:endY="51.91"
                    android:type="linear">
                    <item android:offset="0" android:color="#38FFFFFF" />
                    <item android:offset="1" android:color="#00FFFFFF" />
                </gradient>
            </aapt:attr>
        </path>

        <!-- The crown: the top two edges, caught hard. -->
        <path
            android:pathData="M31.08 37.27 L54 27.14 L76.92 37.27"
            android:strokeColor="#66FFFFFF"
            android:strokeWidth="1.11"
            android:strokeLineCap="round"
            android:strokeLineJoin="round" />

        <!-- The shade under the waist. -->
        <path android:pathData="M0 0h108v108H0Z">
            <aapt:attr name="android:fillColor">
                <gradient
                    android:startX="54"
                    android:startY="45.15"
                    android:endX="54"
                    android:endY="85.37"
                    android:type="linear">
                    <item android:offset="0" android:color="#00000000" />
                    <item android:offset="1" android:color="#4D00150F" />
                </gradient>
            </aapt:attr>
        </path>
    </group>

    <!-- The rim: a stroke on the silhouette, lit at the apex and gone by y63. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M54 23.6 L80.1 34.7 V54.3 c0 16.14 -11.17 27 -26.1 30.1 c-14.94 -3.1 -26.1 -13.96 -26.1 -30.1 V34.7 Z"
        android:strokeWidth="1.0"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round">
        <aapt:attr name="android:strokeColor">
            <gradient
                android:startX="54"
                android:startY="23.6"
                android:endX="54"
                android:endY="63.17"
                android:type="linear">
                <item android:offset="0" android:color="#E6F2FFFB" />
                <item android:offset="0.5" android:color="#33AEFFE9" />
                <item android:offset="1" android:color="#0058E4BD" />
            </gradient>
        </aapt:attr>
    </path>

    <!-- Near wall of the opening: in shadow, offset toward the light. -->
    <group android:translateX="-0.38" android:translateY="-0.5">
        <path
            android:fillColor="#8000110C"
            android:pathData="M56.6 56.1 V63 a2.6 2.6 0 0 1 -5.2 0 V56.1 A7 7 0 1 1 56.6 56.1 Z" />
    </group>

    <!-- Far wall: lit chamfer, one notch above the plate's lightest tone. -->
    <group android:translateX="0.5" android:translateY="0.63">
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FF96FBE1"
            android:pathData="M56.6 56.1 V63 a2.6 2.6 0 0 1 -5.2 0 V56.1 A7 7 0 1 1 56.6 56.1 Z" />
    </group>

    <!-- The opening itself, in the ground colour. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF03170F"
        android:pathData="M56.6 56.1 V63 a2.6 2.6 0 0 1 -5.2 0 V56.1 A7 7 0 1 1 56.6 56.1 Z" />

    <!-- The specular: light caught on the far wall, inside the opening's upper left. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M48.12 47.85 a6.5 6.5 0 0 1 9.25 -3.37"
        android:strokeColor="#80B9FFE9"
        android:strokeWidth="0.88"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />
    </group>
</vector>
